    "title": "Quickly Check Your Public IP",
    "publishedAt": "2026-03-24",
    "updatedAt": "2026-03-24",
    "author": "MvL",
    "summary": "Quickly Check Your Public IP.",
    "category": "Linux",
    "image": "/images/blog/public_ip.jpg",
    "content": "If you’re hosting services at home like Home Assistant, a media server, or a private cloud it’s often useful to know your current public IP address. Instead of logging into your router or using a browser, just run this in your terminal:\n\n```bash\ncurl https://ipinfo.io/ip\n```\n\nDo you use small commands like this in your homelab?\n\n![pbs-screenshot](/images/blog/public_ip.jpg)",
